ify and put forward  those popular policies um just  i've spoken to peter bundelson over the  last few days he of course the former  paul mp you were talking earlier about  the disappointing result in the harlem  pool  he says jeremy corbyn is still casting a  dark cloud  he's largely responsible for some of the  losses that we've seen do you accept  that  long long corbin if you like is  affecting labour's chances  still well  we won hartlepool twice under jeremy  corbyn's leadership  and importantly with a bigger proportion  of the vote i mean you can't say that  jeremy is responsible for the hartley  pool result  the disaffection in post-industrial  britain long predates jeremy's  leadership and we have to look at the  roots of it  let's talk a little bit about kierstarma  and what he needs to do in your view  going forward you talked a bit about  policy and do you think that  and there is a wider strategy issue that  kia starman needs to do  talking a bit more about his vision john  mcdonnell for example saying that some  of those candidates were sent out naked  with no vision  no policies is that something that you  would agree with  i think that kiss darman is to go back  to what he said when he was elected  as leader and he wants to build yes  on some of the policies which we were  talking about in 2019  it is important that candid candidates  can talk about the labor party's vision  and talk about our policies  is it right that angela rainer should  lose her job as party champ  i said earlier i think it's baffling why  he sacked  angela rayna she didn't take any of the  big decisions around hartlepool  and we've not heard anywhere in the  country people  saying they didn't vote labour because  of angela rayna  what do you think it um says about  kirsten's leadership  if the first thing that he does is to  reach out and sac angela rainer who of  course is a  you know working class woman she she's  from the north  some people would say that she's the  kind of 